course: dictionary
lesson: 15568
title: Surveyor: measure, map and check
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A surveyor is a person whose job is to measure land and make maps or plans of it. Surveyors use tools, angles and distances to get the measurements right. «The surveyor measured the field and drew a map of it.» The word tells you the job, and the sentence tells you what the job involves.
explain: A surveyor can also check a building. «Before Mum bought the house, a surveyor checked the walls for cracks.» This is a different kind of surveyor. They look closely at the building to see what condition it is in, and they often do this before someone buys it.
explain: Read the words around surveyor to find its meaning. Words like measured, map, cracks and condition are clues. Ask yourself: what does this person do? Then check your idea by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A surveyor is a person who measures land or checks buildings.
fact: «The surveyor measured the field and drew a map of it.» This is a land surveyor.
fact: «The surveyor's report said the roof needed mending.» A report is a written account of what the surveyor found.
fact: «A surveyor checked the ship before it sailed.» A surveyor can also be an official who inspects things, such as ships.
fact: Surveyors use measuring tools, angles and distances, which you may also meet in maths and geography lessons.
exercise: «The surveyor measured the field and drew a map of it.» What is a surveyor? | A person who sells houses | *A person whose job is to measure land and make maps | A person who cooks food in a café | A farmer who grows wheat
exercise: «Before Mum bought the house, a surveyor checked the walls for cracks.» Why did the surveyor check the walls? | To paint the walls | To count the windows | To take photos for a magazine | *To see what condition the building was in
exercise: «A surveyor checked the ship before it sailed.» Which word in this sentence names the thing the surveyor inspected? | sailed | *ship | before | checked
test: Dad says, «The surveyor's report found damp in the cellar.» What is a surveyor's report about? | A map of a forest | A list of shopping | *A check on the condition of a building | A timetable for trains
test: Which job matches a land surveyor? | *Someone who measures land and makes maps | A baker who makes bread | A bus driver | A teacher who marks spelling tests
exam: Ella's dad hired a surveyor before they bought the house. Why? | To paint the kitchen | *To check the building for damp or cracks | To find a lost cat | To sell the garden
